# API keys. .Renviron holds FOOTBALL_DATA_API_KEY and must never be committed.
.Renviron
.Renviron.*
!.Renviron.example

# Raw pick codes as they arrive. Kept out of git so that pushing before the
# deadline cannot publish anyone's entry early -- predictions.csv and
# predictions_frozen.csv are the records that count.
data/codes.txt
*.knit.md
*.utf8.md
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The prediction model is private.
#
# This repository is public and the other entrants can read it. Everything
# below stays on your machine only: the model code, its inputs and outputs,
# and MODEL.md, which documents it and contains its predicted table.
#
# NOTE: these files were tracked up to and including commit 33857f4, so they
# remain readable in the repository's history on GitHub. Untracking stops
# future exposure; it does not undo past exposure. See MODEL.md notes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
_MODEL.md
R/model.R
R/model_config.R
R/model_data.R
R/manager_tenure.R
R/simulate.R
run_model.R
tune_model.R
run_simulation.R
analyse_carryover.R
data/model/
R/compete.R
run_compete.R
# render_site() writes MODEL.html at the project root as well as under docs/,
# so both paths need covering. The leading-underscore source file is skipped
# by render_site; these two lines catch anything a stale build leaves behind.
MODEL.html
docs/MODEL.html
